  "description": "On reasons to do things",
  "body_html": "<p>What is the <strong>end</strong> goal of my work? Whether that\u2019s my trading, science work, or bike-packing, what\u2019s it all for?</p><p>I used to be pretty utilitarian, where I did things because they were useful. But that\u2019s changed now. It seems that artificial intelligence is quickly being able to solve a lot of the things I set out to do. So my marginal contribution feels small.</p><p>Then I used to things because I enjoyed them. When I went about doing something, I just said fuck it, I don\u2019t really know what the end goal is. I\u2019ll do it because I like it. But that\u2019s changed because things started to feel a bit meaningless when I did this to the extreme.</p><p>So now, I\u2019ve done another reframe. By process of elimination, I\u2019ve had to find the final reason to do things. </p><p>I am now doing things so that I can <em>improve</em> myself.</p><p>There are three the things I can get from the act of creation. The first thing is the utility of what I create. The second is the pleasure of creating. But these reasons feel weak now in today\u2019s context.</p><p>So the third reason makes the most sense. When create something, I also <em>enhance</em> my own being. My cognition increases. I can write better. I build better social skills when I collaborate with others. I increase my capacity for symbolic reasoning. I better my motor skills with my hands. I become a better empiricist. I write better.</p><p>I don\u2019t know whether enhancing oneself is the final boss of reasons to do things. But I can\u2019t think of anything else right now!</p>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
